# Operator-only settings. Never accept these through a crawl request.
# Two modes; pick exactly one. Normal mode is unchanged when these settings are
# all unset, or only CRAWLX_EGRESS_MODE=proxy is set. Partial namespace settings
# are rejected.
#
#   CRAWLX_EGRESS_MODE=netns           privileged: root worker, host nft policy
#   CRAWLX_EGRESS_MODE=netns-rootless  rootless: ordinary-user worker, no root
#
# Required fixed executables (both modes):
#   /usr/bin/python3 (3.12 or newer), /usr/bin/unshare, /usr/bin/setpriv,
#   /usr/sbin/ip, /usr/sbin/nft
# Rootless additionally: /usr/bin/mount, /usr/bin/newuidmap, /usr/bin/newgidmap
#   (file-capability tools from shadow-utils), user.max_user_namespaces > 0, and
#   /etc/subuid + /etc/subgid ranges for the worker's user covering 65535 ids
#   (e.g. `ws:524288:65536`). No root, sudo, CAP_NET_ADMIN or host nft is used.
#
# Install the helper (privileged: root-owned; rootless: owned by root or by the
# worker user). Every parent directory must be a non-symlink, owned by root (or
# by the worker in rootless mode), with neither group nor world write permission:
#   install -m 0755 deploy/isolation/crawlx-netns-helper.py /usr/local/libexec/crawlx-netns-helper.py
CRAWLX_EGRESS_MODE=netns-rootless
CRAWLX_NETNS_HELPER=/usr/local/libexec/crawlx-netns-helper.py
# Privileged: HOST uid/gid of a dedicated browser identity (nonzero).
# Rootless:   NAMESPACE-internal ids in 1..=65534; the helper maps them onto the
#             worker's subuid/subgid range, so the kernel identity is e.g.
#             524288+id-1 and never the worker or root.
CRAWLX_NETNS_BROWSER_UID=1000
CRAWLX_NETNS_BROWSER_GID=1000
#
# Common contract. Namespace mode refuses attached CDP, retained/named profiles,
# visible windows, and the CI --no-sandbox switch (Chromium's own sandbox stays on).
# Configure the actual Chromium ELF executable, not a shell wrapper: its
# device/inode is verified after exec. The host's existing per-browser loopback
# egress proxy remains authoritative. Only filesystem Unix sockets bridge
# namespaces. No veth, host route, default route, UDP, DNS TCP/53, or IPv6 packet
# allowance exists; the in-namespace nft policy is exact and rechecked before
# Chromium is released. CDP is relayed exclusively to worker loopback. The
# anonymous namespace dies with its process group, and a kernel pidfd kills the
# group if the worker dies without Drop. Chromium runs without capabilities,
# supplementary groups, or new privileges. A hostile page cannot change the
# firewall or route table: nft/ip need CAP_NET_ADMIN, which Chromium never holds.
#
# Privileged mode: the worker runs as root (process-group cleanup authority) and
# Chromium as the configured host identity. This does not isolate host files.
#
# Rootless mode: the worker owns a user namespace (namespace root == worker),
# so no capability exists outside it. Chromium runs under a distinct subordinate
# kernel identity inside a private mount namespace: its profile is a size-bounded
# tmpfs (512 MiB, 131072 inodes) over the owned temporary profile directory that
# vanishes with the namespace, and the Chromium install directory is bind-mounted
# read-only inside it. The helper and the worker verify, from /proc, that the
# browser identity never aliases the worker's uid/gid. Host files readable by the
# worker are not readable by the subordinate identity unless world-readable.
#
# Parent verification commands:
#   python3 -I deploy/isolation/test_netns_helper.py
#   # real rootless proof as an ordinary user (fails, never skips, when opted in
#   # and a prerequisite is missing):
#   CRAWLX_RUN_NETNS_ROOTLESS_ACCEPTANCE=1 CRAWLX_CHROMIUM_PATH=/absolute/Chromium \
#     python3 -I deploy/isolation/test_netns_helper.py RootlessAcceptance
#   CRAWLX_RUN_NETNS_ROOTLESS_ACCEPTANCE=1 CRAWLX_CHROMIUM_PATH=/absolute/Chromium \
#     cargo test -p crawlx-browser --test netns_rootless -- --nocapture
#   # privileged proof, root only:
#   CRAWLX_RUN_NETNS_ACCEPTANCE=1 CRAWLX_CHROMIUM_PATH=/absolute/Chromium \
#     CRAWLX_NETNS_BROWSER_UID=65534 CRAWLX_NETNS_BROWSER_GID=65534 \
#     python3 -I deploy/isolation/test_netns_helper.py PrivilegedAcceptance
